\vspace{1cm}
This supplement retains the complete predecessor article on causal posterior
pooling, integrated continuation curvature, overlapping noisy sensing,
stratified acquisition and finite-precision execution. Its mathematical pages
follow unchanged, with their own numbering and bibliography.

\medskip
The current main article proves the charged-clock acquired-geometry theorem
and identifies the precise mechanisms inherited from this text. Preservation
of the complete text does not make its results new claims of the current
revision. The adaptive-refinement and continuation article is retained
separately as Supplement T, and the earlier technical article as Supplement S.

\medskip
This supplement is part of the source-bound submission packet. It is not an
independently published article or a certificate of mathematical correctness.
